From: Kevin Cahalan <kevinacahalan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: k3-r5: keep split-mode cores powered on stop

On the BeagleBone AI-64 (J721E), stopping a main-domain R5F core in split
mode asks the device manager to power the core module off. It answers
with a NACK (module-reset assert failed, -19), and the next start fails
the same way, so the core cannot be restarted without a reboot.

Do what the driver already does on AM64, on every SoC: assert the local
reset and leave the module powered. This kernel is only built for the
BeagleBone AI-64. The 6.18 Debian image uses the same change in
beagle-linux/kernel/k3_r5_rproc.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific workaround]
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/ti_k3_r5_remoteproc.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/ti_k3_r5_remoteproc.c
@@ -331,11 +331,6 @@
 static int k3_r5_split_reset(struct k3_r5_core *core)
 {
 	int ret;
-	struct k3_r5_rproc *kproc;
-	const struct k3_r5_soc_data *soc_data;
-
-	kproc = core->rproc->priv;
-	soc_data = kproc->cluster->soc_data;
 
 	ret = reset_control_assert(core->reset);
 	if (ret) {
@@ -344,24 +339,15 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	/* On AM64 devices power-down of core1 in r5f cluster, even when core0
-	 * is on randomly gets the lpsc stuck in transition state and makes the core
-	 * un-usable. So as a work around keep the power state on with reset
-	 * asserted.
+	/*
+	 * Keep the module powered with the local reset asserted. On AM64,
+	 * powering down core1 while core0 is on can leave the LPSC stuck in
+	 * transition. On J721E the device manager refuses the power-down of a
+	 * split-mode core (-ENODEV), and the core cannot be started again
+	 * after that. k3_r5_split_release() asks for the device again, which
+	 * is harmless while it is already on.
 	 */
-	if (soc_data->single_cpu_mode)
-		return ret;
-
-	ret = core->ti_sci->ops.dev_ops.put_device(core->ti_sci,
-						   core->ti_sci_id);
-	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(core->dev, "module-reset assert failed, ret = %d\n",
-			ret);
-		if (reset_control_deassert(core->reset))
-			dev_warn(core->dev, "local-reset deassert back failed\n");
-	}
-
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int k3_r5_split_release(struct k3_r5_core *core)
